<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anwaruddin Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1672–1749</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad Anwaruddin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anwaruddin Khan was Nawab of the Carnatic, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcot">Arcot</a>, from 1744 to 1749, installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-jah-i">Asaf Jah I</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a>. In 1746 his large army was routed by a small French force at the Adyar river, an early sign of the superiority of European-trained troops. He was killed at the Battle of Ambur in 1749 fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanda-sahib">Chanda Sahib</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaffar-jung">Muzaffar Jung</a>, who were backed by the French.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anwaruddin-khan.jpg" alt="Anwaruddin Khan" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Philippoteaux · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Death_of_the_Nabob_of_the_Carnatic_by_Paul_Philippoteaux.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
